# H98 (audit 2026-09-13): npm runs preinstall/install/postinstall for EVERY package in the tree
# by default, so a compromised transitive dependency gets arbitrary code execution at `npm ci`
# time — on the contributor's machine and, worse, on the release host that also holds the store
# credentials and the Android keystore. That is code execution before a single test has run, and
# for a password manager the blast radius is the release path itself.
#
# Nothing in this tree needs an install hook: the only `hasInstallScript` package in
# package-lock.json is esbuild, whose postinstall merely fetches/links a platform binary that npm
# already installs directly as the optional `@esbuild/<platform>` package. Vite and vitest resolve
# it through that package, which is why the suite and the build keep working with hooks off.
#
# Keep this file in lockstep with extension/.npmrc and with the `--ignore-scripts` flags on the
# Dockerfile's and CONTRIBUTING.md's install lines: an install performed from any of those paths
# without it re-opens the same door.
ignore-scripts=true
